{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d travel 3 d travel","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md","fileName":"3D Travel.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Travel","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Navigation","Degrees of Freedom","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d travel 3 d travel","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md","fileName":"3D Travel.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Travel","heading":"3D Travel","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"3D travel is the motor component of [[Navigation]]: moving from the current location to a target or moving in a desired direction.\n\nTravel can be physical or virtual and actively controlled or system-controlled. Common task types are exploration, goal-directed search, and precise local maneuvering. Their requirements differ: exploration benefits from interruptible continuous control, search can use target-based movement, and maneuvering needs fine adjustment.\n\nTechnique choice should also consider distance, path curvature, target visibility, required [[Degrees of Freedom]], accuracy, and other tasks performed during movement. Because travel often supports a more important task, it should demand little unnecessary attention.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Navigation","Degrees of Freedom","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d travel 3 d travel","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Travel.md","fileName":"3D Travel.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Travel","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Navigation","Degrees of Freedom","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}